@using InventoryManagerApp.Data
@using InventoryManagerApp.Components.Services
@using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore
@page "/About"

<PageTitle>About</PageTitle>

<!-- This page explains the application -->

<div class="container mt-4">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <br />
    <h3>About Inventory Manager v2</h3>
    <hr />
    <p>
        This application is a project for a Computer Science Capstone course. It is a direct conversion from a previous project in CS-360 Mobile Programming where
        a Java based Inventory Management application was developed to assist warehouse operations. The original Java project has been
        successfully migrated and rebuilt in .NET 8 using the Blazor Server framework in C#.
    </p>
    <p>
        The application is designed to provide an intuitive, responsive interface for managing inventory, user accounts, and system roles.
        It incorporates modern user authentication, role-based authorization, and several core features to streamline inventory management
        tasks for warehouses.
    </p>

    <h3>Key Features</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>User Authentication and Role-Based Authorization:</strong> Secure login and role management for administrators and warehouse staff.</li>
        <li><strong>Inventory Management Module:</strong> Manage inventory items with detailed item records, including SKU, UPC, cost, price, and quantity.</li>
        <li><strong>Low Stock Notifications:</strong> An efficient AVL Tree algorithm powers low stock warnings with color-coded banners for warning and critical levels.</li>
        <li><strong>Role Management:</strong> Administrators can create, assign, and manage roles with fine-grained control over access to different parts of the application.</li>
        <li><strong>User Management:</strong> Manage user accounts with options to create, edit, and delete users, as well as assign roles.</li>
        <li><strong>Account Settings:</strong> Allow users to update their own account details, such as passwords and profile information.</li>
        <li><strong>Responsive and Intuitive Interface:</strong> The application is built with a responsive design, ensuring usability across devices of different screen sizes.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Technical Highlights</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Rebuilt in .NET 8 using Blazor Server for modern web application architecture.</li>
        <li>Uses Entity Framework Core for database interactions.</li>
        <li>Implements Identity Framework for secure authentication and authorization.</li>
        <li>Efficient AVL Tree algorithm for fast and reliable low stock detection and notifications.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        This application showcases the integration of software engineering concepts, data structures, and modern web development techniques.
        It serves as an example of how existing projects can be migrated to newer technologies while maintaining and enhancing core functionality.
    </p>
    <hr />
    <p><strong>Author:</strong>  James Frost </p>
    <p>   January, 2025  </p>
</div>
